PS5 HFR1 / CS2 Nuke / Full CS2 L3 and zero root CAT A/B/A
2026-11-07. Original CS2 -insecure, local Nuke 1x, first person, seek 10048
(~02:38), 10-second warm-up, reseek and 15-second measurement. System RADV
26.0.8, stock MP1, 1080p240 X11. All scored notifications are Flip. FPS/tail
metrics describe displayed cadence using unique Present UST/MSC.

CS2 was placed in the dedicated full-mask shareable CAT group in all phases.
Exact game membership was checked on both sides of the score. Root mask
ffff/ffff in A1/A2, zero/zero throughout the scored B window. No CPU affinity
or memory-bandwidth schema change. Zero prevents new allocations by the root
class, and does not merge the two physical 4 MiB L3 domains. Other classes may
hit already-installed lines. System code in the game context uses that class.

A smoke check separately verified both the zero root write and automatic
restoration by an independent 2-second system timer. B used a 28-second
watchdog and restored full root explicitly after the last sample. An earlier
B launch was excluded before any zero write because Pulse did not supply a
PID for the game's own PipeWire playback. The scored B verified its owner via
PipeWire's authenticated PID and zero active recording. No Discord client
was running. A1 and the scored B/A2 used separate identical resctrl mounts
because the aborted phase cleaned up. No boot, kernel or firmware change.

CS2 closed normally. Configs were restored byte-identically. Test group
removed, resctrl unmounted, watchdogs stopped. No new matching MCE/MSR/GPU/OOM
kernel events. One B repeat measures a candidate, not reproducibility.
Linux resctrl: https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/resctrl.html
AMD PQoS: https://www.amd.com/content/dam/amd/en/documents/processor-tech-docs/other/56375_1_03_PUB.pdf#page=18

